CLI arguments for `trusty-embedderd`.

Why: clap derive is the workspace standard for all trusty-* binaries. What: `--stdio` for the sidecar transport (piped stdin/stdout), `--http` for the TCP listener, `--socket` for the UDS listener. `--stdio` is mutually exclusive with `--http` and `--socket`. `--batch-size` and `--batch-window-ms` configure the `BatchQueue` coalescing window. Test: `clap::Parser::try_parse_from` in unit tests.

Usage: trusty-embedderd [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --stdio
          Run in stdio sidecar mode: read JSON-RPC requests from stdin, write responses to stdout. Mutually exclusive with --http and --socket. This is the transport used when trusty-search auto-spawns trusty-embedderd as a child process (issue #110 Phase 2 default).
          
          Why: avoids socket-file management — the parent owns the pipe handles and the child exits automatically when the parent closes its end.

      --http <HTTP_ADDR>
          TCP address to listen on for HTTP (host:port).
          
